        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: MedStar Georgetown University Hospital, Howard University Hospital, The New Freedmen's Clinic, Howard University College of Medicine\n- People: Michael Zasloff\n- Places: Georgetown neighborhood, Northwest Quadrant of Washington, D.C., Washington, D.C., Griffith Stadium\n- Roles: Scientific Director\n- Concepts: not-for-profit, acute care, teaching hospital, research facility, free student-run health care clinic\n\nFacts:\n- Howard University Hospital, previously known as Freedmen's Hospital, is a major hospital in Washington, D.C., built on the site of the previous Griffith Stadium.\n- In the summer of 2009, The New Freedmen's Clinic first opened as a free student-run health care clinic affiliated with Howard University Hospital and Howard University College of Medicine.\n- MedStar Georgetown University Hospital is a not-for-profit, acute care teaching and research facility located in the Georgetown neighborhood of the Northwest Quadrant of Washington, D.C.\n- Michael Zasloff is the Scientific Director of the MedStar-Georgetown Transplant Institute at Georgetown University Hospital.",
